traces.inference_trace:
The program renders the image row by row in parallel threads and writes a binary PBM to stdout.

**Coordinates and iteration.** It uses the usual mapping for this benchmark:
- Each pixel maps to `c = (2x/N − 1.5) + i(2y/N − 1.0)`.
- Each step updates `Zi = 2·Zr·Zi + Ci`, then `Zr = Tr − Ti + Cr`, then `Tr = Zr²`, `Ti = Zi²`.
- The iteration cap is 50.

**Vectorisation and escape test.** Pixels are processed 8 at a time, one byte of output per group, using vectors of 8 doubles. Each lane has an "escaped" flag. The flag is set the first time `Tr + Ti > 4` and is never cleared. This latching matters: once a value escapes, later squarings can overflow to `inf` and then become `NaN`, and `NaN > 4` is false. Because the flag never resets, those lanes still count as escaped. The loop stops early once all 8 lanes have escaped.

**Output format.**
- A pixel's bit is 1 if it never escaped.
- Bits are packed high bit first.
- Padding bits past column N in the last byte of each row are 0.
- The header is `P4\nN N\n`.

**Floating-point consistency.** FMA contraction is turned off, so boundary pixels come out the same as a plain step-by-step evaluation.

```cpp
#pragma GCC optimize("O3,fp-contract=off")
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstdint>
#include <vector>
#include <thread>
#include <atomic>

typedef double v8 __attribute__((vector_size(64)));
typedef long long m8 __attribute__((vector_size(64)));

static int N, bpr;
static unsigned char* buf;
static std::atomic<int> nextRow(0);

static void work() {
    double inv = 2.0 / N;
    while (true) {
        int y = nextRow.fetch_add(1);
        if (y >= N) break;
        double ci = (double)y * inv - 1.0;
        unsigned char* out = buf + (size_t)y * bpr;
        for (int bx = 0; bx < bpr; bx++) {
            v8 Cr;
            for (int k = 0; k < 8; k++) Cr[k] = (double)(bx * 8 + k) * inv - 1.5;
            v8 Ci = {ci, ci, ci, ci, ci, ci, ci, ci};
            v8 Zr = {0}, Zi = {0}, Tr = {0}, Ti = {0};
            m8 esc = {0};
            v8 four = {4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4};
            for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {
                Zi = 2.0 * Zr * Zi + Ci;
                Zr = Tr - Ti + Cr;
                Tr = Zr * Zr;
                Ti = Zi * Zi;
                esc |= (m8)(Tr + Ti > four);
                long long a = esc[0] & esc[1] & esc[2] & esc[3] & esc[4] & esc[5] & esc[6] & esc[7];
                if (a) break;
            }
            unsigned char b = 0;
            for (int k = 0; k < 8; k++) {
                int x = bx * 8 + k;
                if (x < N && !esc[k]) b |= (unsigned char)(0x80 >> k);
            }
            out[bx] = b;
        }
    }
}

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
    N = argc > 1 ? atoi(argv[1]) : 200;
    if (N < 0) N = 0;
    bpr = (N + 7) / 8;
    std::vector<unsigned char> data((size_t)bpr * N + 1);
    buf = data.data();
    unsigned nt = std::thread::hardware_concurrency();
    if (nt == 0) nt = 4;
    std::vector<std::thread> ts;
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < nt; i++) ts.emplace_back(work);
    for (auto& t : ts) t.join();
    printf("P4\n%d %d\n", N, N);
    fflush(stdout);
    fwrite(buf, 1, (size_t)bpr * N, stdout);
    fflush(stdout);
    return 0;
}
```

